<title>USA: Bio-Vascular to file for new Peri-Strips.</title>
<headline>Bio-Vascular to file for new Peri-Strips.</headline>
<dateline>ST. PAUL, Minn. 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bio-Vascular Inc said Tuesday it would soon file an application with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for clearance to market a new version of Peri-Strips, used in lung volume reduction operations.</p>
<p>Bio-Vascular also said it would file to market Tissue-Guard, a tissue repair product, as an intra-cardiac device used in surgery.</p>
<p>The company said it was also working with Mentor Corp to develop urology applications for Tissue-Guard.</p>
<p>&quot;Finally we are evaluating applications for Tissue-Guard in colo-rectal, bladder, stomach and opthalmic surgeries,&quot; John Karcanes, president, said in a statement.</p>
<p>Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787</p>
